<!DOCTYPE Menu PUBLIC "-//freedesktop//DTD Menu 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/menu-spec/menu-1.0.dtd">

<!-- A "Tenstorrent" section in the application menu.

     This is a MERGE file: it does not define a whole menu, it grafts one
     submenu onto whatever the desktop already builds. Anything whose desktop
     entry carries Categories=...;X-Tenstorrent; lands in it.

     X-Tenstorrent, not Tenstorrent. The Desktop Entry Specification reserves
     unprefixed category names for its own registered list (Science, Development,
     Utility, ...); everything else MUST carry the X- prefix. A bare
     "Tenstorrent" would be an invalid category, and desktop-file-validate says
     so.

     WHO OWNS THIS FILE. Right now, tt-bio-demo -- because it is the only
     Tenstorrent application packaged this way. The moment a second one ships
     (tt-toplike, tt-local-generator, tt-station), this file and
     tenstorrent.directory must move into a shared package that they all
     depend on. Two packages shipping the same path is a dpkg conflict on
     install, which this project has already hit once with helpers.sh -- see
     the note in debian/tt-bio-demo.install. Moving it later is a one-time
     Replaces/Breaks; discovering it at a conference is not. -->

<Menu>
  <Name>Applications</Name>

  <Menu>
    <Name>Tenstorrent</Name>
    <Directory>tenstorrent.directory</Directory>
    <Include>
      <Category>X-Tenstorrent</Category>
    </Include>
  </Menu>

</Menu>
